body:
Nice work, although I noticed one small issue in my use case. Whenever I bake a scene and rotate the root object, it will cause the specular lighting to break, but not the normal maps.

Test project with example scene:
[test_lightmap_directional_specular_lobe_2025-11-09_16-04-04.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23442929/test_lightmap_directional_specular_lobe_2025-11-09_16-04-04.zip)

Here is a screenshot of the issue (no patch):
![godot windows editor x86_64 mono_c8kYggJSUi](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/511fbda2-903e-4e3d-83e4-29201dcedc17)

Here is a screenshot with it fixed (patch):
![godot windows editor x86_64 mono_LXxSztalK5](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ac2be875-6fd4-47a3-aa5b-7e57765f5fb4)

Here is the patch to fix the issue in Forward+:
```diff
diff --git a/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/forward_clustered/scene_forward_clustered.glsl b/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/forward_clustered/scene_forward_clustered.glsl
index f9f2d6fc1a..ab8c7f00a3 100644
--- a/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/forward_clustered/scene_forward_clustered.glsl
+++ b/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/forward_clustered/scene_forward_clustered.glsl
@@ -1767,9 +1767,9 @@ void fragment_shader(in SceneData scene_data) {
 
 				vec3 l1 = (l1_r + l1_g + l1_b) / 3.0;
 				vec3 lightmap_direction = normalize(l1);
 
-				vec3 L_view = hvec3(mat3(scene_data.view_matrix) * lightmap_direction);
+				vec3 L_view = hvec3(inverse(lightmaps.data[ofs].normal_xform) * lightmap_direction);
 
 				vec3 f0 = F0(metallic, specular, albedo);
 
 				// Discard diffuse light from this fake light, as we're only interested in its specular light output.
```
